00:32:24.220 --> 00:32:31.040
of complaints. You don't really take citizenship seriously. You might. But if you're an international

00:32:31.040 --> 00:32:35.380
student, if you've traveled the world, if you know the challenges of being an immigrant, I mean

00:32:35.380 --> 00:32:41.220
citizenship is important, right? It has privileges and rights that come with it, and it's not easy to

00:32:41.220 --> 00:32:44.700
get. I mean, the U.S., it's not easy to get citizenship, but there are countries where you

00:32:44.700 --> 00:32:51.360
have to be residents for like 30 years. The local populace has to vote on your citizenship, and they

00:32:51.360 --> 00:32:55.580
have to approve your citizenship. There are places where you have to speak a certain language, show a

00:32:55.580 --> 00:33:00.500
certain proficiency. All these, citizenship is not easy, and so whether it's back then or here, like

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:04.280
We should know and realize that citizenship is important.

00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:11.800
And here, Paul is saying that Gentile Christians, people who, even though they don't come from that Jewish background,

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:18.560
they were fellow citizens in the kingdom of God, in the people of God.

00:33:20.220 --> 00:33:21.720
That they're not second-class citizens.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:26.600
It's not like they have some provisional status, that they don't have an intermediate status.

00:33:26.600 --> 00:33:29.120
They are full citizens in this kingdom.

00:33:30.080 --> 00:33:33.940
And furthermore, not just citizenship status, but now they're part of the family.

00:33:34.700 --> 00:33:38.240
He says that you are fellow members of God's household.

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:41.080
So it's not like you can be distant from one another.

00:33:41.180 --> 00:33:42.640
It's like you are siblings now.

00:33:43.380 --> 00:33:47.320
That's why we talk all the time about this family relationship.

00:33:48.620 --> 00:33:55.180
And they're now all a part of this, and then God is building them together as one temple in the Lord.

00:33:55.180 --> 00:33:58.660
It's helpful to realize that

00:33:58.660 --> 00:34:01.520
There's one temple that's being built up

00:34:01.520 --> 00:34:05.680
And it all shares the same foundation of Christ

00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:09.910
It's not like, you know

00:34:09.910 --> 00:34:11.590
The Jewish Christians have one foundation

00:34:11.590 --> 00:34:13.930
And the Gentile Christians have another foundation

00:34:13.930 --> 00:34:14.830
Right?

00:34:14.850 --> 00:34:17.510
It's not like you're adding on to your house

00:34:17.510 --> 00:34:20.210
And then this new addition doesn't share the same foundation

00:34:20.210 --> 00:34:22.450
As the original structure

00:34:22.450 --> 00:34:23.470
Some of you guys rent

00:34:23.470 --> 00:34:24.750
And you don't care what I'm talking about

00:34:24.750 --> 00:34:25.890
Other people, you own a house

00:34:25.890 --> 00:34:27.050
You know what I'm talking about, right?

00:34:27.050 --> 00:34:28.830
It's one foundation.

00:34:29.170 --> 00:34:31.830
He's saying whether you're Jewish, whether you're Gentile,

00:34:31.930 --> 00:34:35.870
we share one foundation on which this family of God,

00:34:35.950 --> 00:34:38.610
this temple is being built up together.

00:34:38.950 --> 00:34:41.610
And God is the one who is doing this building.

00:34:44.300 --> 00:34:47.780
You know, this is the core of why our church says

00:34:47.780 --> 00:34:51.600
that we want to be a transcultural spiritual family

00:34:51.600 --> 00:34:55.880
reaching our neighbors, the nations, and the next generation.

00:34:55.880 --> 00:35:05.420
Like, why do we think it's important to be transcultural, to be above just regular human cultures, to strive for this gospel culture?

00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:12.360
Why is it important that we try to go through the difficulties of getting to know people who are different from us and incorporating them into the family of God?

00:35:12.420 --> 00:35:18.560
Why is that? It's because of what Christ has done here, what God is doing here, right?

00:35:18.580 --> 00:35:24.700
He's saying that no matter what your background is, you are fellow citizens and part of the household of God.

00:35:24.700 --> 00:35:27.960
I love Edward's testimony, right?

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:28.840
He's saying like, what?

00:35:29.480 --> 00:35:31.240
He's like, yo, I'm from China.

00:35:31.380 --> 00:35:33.780
I think you said the guy was from Nigeria, but we are brothers and crew.

00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:34.860
We're part of the same family.

00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:36.700
We're part of the same family.

00:35:37.020 --> 00:35:38.000
Some of you don't know.

00:35:38.180 --> 00:35:43.080
If you've ever traveled to a non-English speaking country and you hear other people speaking English, there is a joy.

00:35:43.200 --> 00:35:43.740
I don't know for you.

00:35:44.020 --> 00:35:48.540
It bubbles up in my heart because I'm like, oh, my gosh, there's another one of us, you know?

00:35:49.080 --> 00:35:50.320
That's what it's like, right?

00:35:50.320 --> 00:35:54.000
You could be so different, but when you're in this family, it's like, oh, this is a brother.

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:54.960
This is a sister.

00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:58.880
We are part of the same family, no matter what differences we have.

00:35:59.720 --> 00:36:03.120
And the important thing to see here is that we are not creating.

00:36:03.340 --> 00:36:06.260
We are not making and forcing this diverse reality.

00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:08.040
God has done it.

00:36:08.680 --> 00:36:14.280
Jesus has gotten rid of the hostility, and God is building us together, fitting us together.

00:36:14.840 --> 00:36:15.780
God is doing that work.

00:36:15.860 --> 00:36:17.980
We are participating in what God is doing.

00:36:19.140 --> 00:36:23.040
We are making real the reality that God has already given to us.

00:36:23.120 --> 00:36:23.700
That's the difference.

00:36:24.960 --> 00:36:28.840
And so here we see that, and the question is, well, how do we practically pursue this?

00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:30.880
Just a couple of things for us as we close.

00:36:31.900 --> 00:36:37.460
You know, one is that we have to repent when we fail to embrace this kind of unity.

00:36:40.480 --> 00:36:44.460
This unity here is talking about the Jews and the Gentile Christians,

00:36:44.600 --> 00:36:49.820
but this is the core of what extends to all the kind of diversity we want to see in the church.

00:36:49.980 --> 00:36:55.940
Like I mentioned, that could be political, that could be generational, that could be racial.

00:36:56.120 --> 00:36:58.420
That could be gender differences, right?

00:36:58.740 --> 00:37:03.240
It's easy to have a suspicion, anger, hostility towards different groups right now.

00:37:03.800 --> 00:37:08.280
But here we say, no, all of these people are part of the same family that share the same foundation.

00:37:08.380 --> 00:37:13.000
We have to strive to make, to realize that, the reality that God has given us.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:17.800
And I think the first step, I think, is to be honest and to repent.

00:37:18.500 --> 00:37:19.960
That it's not easy to do that.

00:37:20.940 --> 00:37:22.560
And that you often struggle with that.

00:37:22.780 --> 00:37:24.200
I often struggle with that.

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:25.600
Right?

00:37:25.980 --> 00:37:26.800
We all want to pretend.

00:37:26.900 --> 00:37:28.060
This is what is so funny.

00:37:28.220 --> 00:37:31.920
Like, so many people want to pretend like they're not prejudiced.

00:37:33.080 --> 00:37:36.180
And it's like the reality is like, dude, we're all prejudiced, right?

00:37:36.440 --> 00:37:39.920
You own up to it and say, God, I have a propensity to want to be comfortable,

00:37:40.520 --> 00:37:43.020
to be like the people who are like me, right?

00:37:43.380 --> 00:37:47.080
And to say, God, it's hard for me to like and love and serve and invest in people

00:37:47.080 --> 00:37:49.860
who are genuinely and really different from me.

00:37:49.860 --> 00:37:52.220
You own up to that and say, I failed, God.

00:37:52.220 --> 00:37:55.220
that in reality, I'm much more like

00:37:55.220 --> 00:37:57.900
these university marketing groups

00:37:57.900 --> 00:38:00.940
that would be okay with shallow diversity

00:38:00.940 --> 00:38:03.840
rather than fighting for real deep unity.

00:38:04.500 --> 00:38:06.660
And to say, God, I'm sorry, I mess up in that.

00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:07.820
I can't be bothered.

00:38:07.920 --> 00:38:09.660
I'm too busy with other things in my life, God.

00:38:09.800 --> 00:38:11.860
And I have let other things be priorities

00:38:11.860 --> 00:38:13.420
over the things that are priority for you.

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:15.400
To recognize that and to acknowledge that,

00:38:15.920 --> 00:38:16.980
say, God, I failed for that.

00:38:20.110 --> 00:38:23.270
Like this, you know, we talk about the wall of hostility.

00:38:23.270 --> 00:38:27.570
be like, did you know, like, when we used to bring people to Detroit, we would do a tour of the city

00:38:27.570 --> 00:38:32.510
to show how it's still functionally segregated in different places. Did you know there's a wall

00:38:32.510 --> 00:38:37.170
in Detroit that used to separate where black people could live and where white people could

00:38:37.170 --> 00:38:43.750
live, right? And that, like, we are in a community and context where there is real separation,

00:38:45.110 --> 00:38:49.570
right? And like I said, there are real differences between different groups. And say, God, you know

00:38:49.570 --> 00:38:57.370
what i have failed to strive for this in my life i failed to really try to love and understand my

00:38:57.370 --> 00:39:03.750
neighbor it's easier for me to just write things off to stereotype people to minimize them and say

00:39:03.750 --> 00:39:09.310
god help me god help me to have your heart forgive me for how small my heart has been that's that's

00:39:09.310 --> 00:39:17.350
step number one step number two is what receiving god's promises with confidence say god i want to

00:39:17.350 --> 00:39:22.810
really trust and hold on. There's no other way this kind of unity can work except that you have

00:39:22.810 --> 00:39:29.550
already made it possible at the cross. And can I say for some of us, that means you have to get over

00:39:29.550 --> 00:39:36.950
yourself. And what I mean by that is some of us, you are plagued with insecurity and self-loathing

00:39:36.950 --> 00:39:42.250
to say like, oh, I don't know if I, if I belong here, I don't know if I can do this. And can I say

00:39:42.250 --> 00:39:47.650
like as certain as your salvation is certain your inclusion into the family is certain

00:39:47.650 --> 00:39:53.470
and to say you cannot let those insecurities rule your life but instead to say god help your

00:39:53.470 --> 00:39:59.290
word and your promise rule my life to say i belong here not because people are nice to me because you

00:39:59.290 --> 00:40:05.750
have made it possible on the cross that gives me all the credibility i need to be a part of your

00:40:05.750 --> 00:40:13.950
family. And some of you, you cannot let those lies and those toxic thoughts rule your life,

00:40:14.050 --> 00:40:18.510
but to say instead, God, give me the faith to hold on to your promises, to say that I am a part of

00:40:18.510 --> 00:40:27.150
your family. And then the third is to do the real work of building unity as we rely on the Lord.

00:40:28.370 --> 00:40:31.590
Like we said, this is not something you can just do out of your own strength.

00:40:32.270 --> 00:40:36.670
Like we all have this natural propensity to preserve ourselves, to prefer ourselves,

00:40:36.670 --> 00:40:39.510
and instead to say, God, I need you to change my heart

00:40:39.510 --> 00:40:42.770
to be selfless and sacrificial like Christ.

00:40:43.370 --> 00:40:45.490
Holy Spirit, I need you to do this work in my heart.

00:40:45.770 --> 00:40:47.750
I could not do it on my own.

00:40:50.760 --> 00:40:52.820
And to say that we really need your help

00:40:52.820 --> 00:40:55.400
and that we can do this because you are already,

00:40:55.540 --> 00:40:58.440
you are doing this work of fitting together your church.

00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:00.300
Help me to be a part of that.

00:41:00.560 --> 00:41:01.880
Strengthen me to do that.

00:41:04.860 --> 00:41:05.780
And that's why in this passage,

00:41:05.880 --> 00:41:07.440
we see that no matter our background,

00:41:07.960 --> 00:41:10.280
you see this beautiful triune picture.

00:41:11.220 --> 00:41:15.300
of God the Son reconciling you to God the Father

00:41:15.300 --> 00:41:16.980
so that by the power of God the Spirit

00:41:16.980 --> 00:41:19.560
that we can be this transcultural people

00:41:19.560 --> 00:41:21.340
that he has called us to be.

00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:23.320
That's why the one thing, again,

00:41:23.400 --> 00:41:25.460
is that we are called to live out the unity

00:41:25.460 --> 00:41:28.600
that God has established for his diverse people.

00:41:35.020 --> 00:41:36.060
And like I said, as we close,

00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:38.760
you have to see that this Christian unity

00:41:38.760 --> 00:41:44.500
is better than that marketing diversity and unity.

00:41:44.500 --> 00:41:47.460
This is a real, real unity.

00:41:47.680 --> 00:41:53.140
And can I tell you just as we close, the joys of having this kind of unity and diversity

00:41:53.140 --> 00:41:56.860
is that the people that it's so easy for us to distance ourselves from,

00:41:57.240 --> 00:42:02.500
like there is something about their perspective and their experience and their background

00:42:02.500 --> 00:42:07.760
that helps them understand God maybe in a deeper and a distinct way than you can.

00:42:08.480 --> 00:42:12.820
And part of the joy of being in a diverse community is that you can be curious.

00:42:13.440 --> 00:42:15.220
And you can be curious to say, you know what?

00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:19.760
Like, how does that help you to understand God in a different way

00:42:19.760 --> 00:42:22.640
that maybe you wouldn't have realized yourself, right?

00:42:23.140 --> 00:42:27.960
Like, the easy benefits of diversity is, like, you get more food, which is great, right?

00:42:27.980 --> 00:42:29.300
I love food, right?

00:42:29.360 --> 00:42:30.500
And that's part of it, right?

00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:34.660
But the diversity of food, I mean, it is just a shallow reflection

00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:38.860
of the greater diversity of increased mature faith that you can have

00:42:38.860 --> 00:42:40.480
as you're in a diverse community.

00:42:41.300 --> 00:42:46.140
You realize, oh, like this group resonates with that aspect of God more deeply,

00:42:46.140 --> 00:42:50.700
and I can learn to tap into that as I hear them, understand them, and get to know them more.

00:42:51.280 --> 00:42:54.720
That I have distinct things, that I can see God in a slightly distinct,

00:42:54.940 --> 00:42:56.580
emphasize these things because of my experience.

00:42:56.840 --> 00:43:00.620
And as you get to know and share and be curious, that's how you build one another up.

00:43:00.820 --> 00:43:03.520
And that's the joy of being able to do that in a diverse community.

00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:10.220
And that's the kind of unity that God desires for us and that he is working in us.

00:43:10.220 --> 00:43:13.800
and that this is a unity that will outlast the ages.

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:17.900
I mean, some of us are so used to shallow unity.

00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:22.640
Like, you are like best bros with people who like the same anime.

00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:24.640
Like, that's great, right?

00:43:24.720 --> 00:43:26.620
You are family with people who like the same sports team.

00:43:26.660 --> 00:43:27.140
That's great.

00:43:27.380 --> 00:43:29.280
You know, in 10,000 years, that won't matter.

00:43:30.120 --> 00:43:32.940
But this unity in Christ, eternal.

00:43:35.060 --> 00:43:38.480
Revelation chapter 7, like, this is John as he sees the vision in heaven.

00:43:38.480 --> 00:44:12.290
And he says, as I looked and behold a great multitude that no one could number from every nation, from all tribes and peoples and languages, standing before the throne and before the Lamb, sorry, before the Lamb, clothed in white robes with palm branches in their hands and crying out with a loud voice, salvation belongs to our God who sits on the throne and to the Lamb.

00:44:12.290 --> 00:44:15.770
for the rest of all

00:44:15.770 --> 00:44:16.490
eternity

00:44:16.490 --> 00:44:19.610
you will spend it with brothers and sisters in Christ

00:44:19.610 --> 00:44:21.750
who are different from you but you will be united

00:44:21.750 --> 00:44:22.890
in worship

00:44:22.890 --> 00:44:25.730
worshiping the only

00:44:25.730 --> 00:44:27.710
God who deserves our trust

00:44:27.710 --> 00:44:29.650
and our praise and that

00:44:29.650 --> 00:44:31.830
is a unity worth fighting

00:44:31.830 --> 00:44:33.410
for and experiencing

00:44:33.410 --> 00:44:35.010
even here now

00:44:35.010 --> 00:44:36.670
let's pray

00:44:36.670 --> 00:44:41.710
Father we thank you

00:44:41.710 --> 00:44:46.100
we thank you that you saw us

00:44:46.100 --> 00:44:48.320
in our pitiful state

00:44:48.320 --> 00:44:50.820
and that you did not

00:44:50.820 --> 00:44:52.900
leave us

00:44:52.900 --> 00:44:54.260
and ignore us

00:44:54.260 --> 00:44:57.420
but you send your son

00:44:57.420 --> 00:45:00.920
to save us

00:45:00.920 --> 00:45:03.000
from the pitiful condition

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:03.620
that we were in.

00:45:04.920 --> 00:45:05.980
That your son lived

00:45:05.980 --> 00:45:07.660
a life we could never have lived.

00:45:08.220 --> 00:45:09.260
Died for all the things

00:45:09.260 --> 00:45:09.820
that we deserved

00:45:09.820 --> 00:45:12.060
and resurrected

00:45:12.060 --> 00:45:13.820
to guarantee to us

00:45:13.820 --> 00:45:15.120
an eternal life in you.

00:45:16.680 --> 00:45:18.620
That it's not by scrambling up

00:45:18.620 --> 00:45:20.020
enough good works

00:45:20.020 --> 00:45:22.680
that we can be reconciled to you

00:45:22.680 --> 00:45:25.940
and that we can just wholeheartedly trust

00:45:25.940 --> 00:45:27.160
in your work for us.

00:45:27.200 --> 00:45:28.540
We thank you that you saw us

00:45:28.540 --> 00:45:29.320
in that pitiful state

00:45:29.320 --> 00:45:32.000
and that you have made possible

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:34.780
to be reconciled with you.

00:45:36.380 --> 00:45:37.280
We thank you, God,

00:45:37.320 --> 00:45:39.220
that you did not leave us there by ourselves,

00:45:39.280 --> 00:45:40.960
but that you brought us into a family,

00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:44.000
a family that spans all generations

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:46.220
and all continents and all peoples.

00:45:48.910 --> 00:45:50.570
That we could be welcomed and included

00:45:50.570 --> 00:45:52.530
to be a part of this temple

00:45:52.530 --> 00:45:53.970
where your Holy Spirit dwells.

00:45:55.390 --> 00:45:57.550
And God, that even now that you are working in us

00:45:57.550 --> 00:46:00.050
so that we can continue to reflect that

00:46:00.050 --> 00:46:00.730
to the world around us.

00:46:00.770 --> 00:46:02.590
Lord, we thank you for the work that you are doing.

00:46:03.590 --> 00:46:06.130
Lord, we ask that you would be gracious to us

00:46:06.130 --> 00:46:06.830
as a church,

00:46:07.410 --> 00:46:09.330
that you would help us to fight

00:46:09.330 --> 00:46:12.230
for this kind of unity that you have made possible.

00:46:13.750 --> 00:46:16.870
Forgive us when our hearts get jaded

00:46:16.870 --> 00:46:19.810
forgive us when we rely on ourselves

00:46:19.810 --> 00:46:21.490
forgive us when we

00:46:21.490 --> 00:46:23.510
revert back to the hostility

00:46:23.510 --> 00:46:25.410
that is so easy to engage in

00:46:25.410 --> 00:46:27.430
and Lord

00:46:27.430 --> 00:46:29.370
instead continue to change us God

00:46:29.370 --> 00:46:31.110
that from positions

00:46:31.110 --> 00:46:33.710
of confident and yet humility

00:46:33.710 --> 00:46:35.850
that you would help us to love

00:46:35.850 --> 00:46:37.970
one another and to love our neighbor

00:46:37.970 --> 00:46:39.330
and to love the nations

00:46:39.330 --> 00:46:40.830
and to love the next generation God

00:46:40.830 --> 00:46:43.370
so that we could be a diverse people

00:46:43.370 --> 00:46:45.050
that reflect your

00:46:45.050 --> 00:46:47.070
multifaceted, ever-reaching

00:46:47.070 --> 00:46:47.910
grace in our lives.

00:46:49.310 --> 00:46:51.170
We need your help. Thank you for your

00:46:51.170 --> 00:46:52.830
goodness. We pray that you would

00:46:52.830 --> 00:46:54.990
let these things sink deeper into our hearts,

00:46:55.050 --> 00:46:56.570
that you would transform us with your word

00:46:56.570 --> 00:46:59.070
and strengthen us to do these things in our

00:46:59.070 --> 00:46:59.450
everyday

00:46:59.450 --> 00:47:02.930
and the opportunities that you give us. We thank you.

00:47:03.010 --> 00:47:04.990
We pray all these things in Jesus' name. Amen.
